TI  - Devising the guidelines: the concept of uniportal video-assisted thoracic 
      surgery-instrumentation and operatory room staff.
PG  - S2079-S2085
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2019.08.69 [doi]
AB  - In the last years, uniportal video-assisted thoracic surgery (VATS) has been 
      gaining more and more popularity, becoming a common procedure in several thoracic 
      centers all over the world not only for minor procedures but also for major and 
      complex cases. This technique combines the advantages of the less invasiveness 
      with the oncological principles of open surgery. A standardization of the 
      different peri- and intraoperative steps can help in the establishment and 
      development of this technique. The aim of this paper is to set the basic steps 
      for operating room set-up and instrumentation for starting or improving a 
      uniportal VATS program in thoracic surgery centers.
CI  - 2019 Journal of Thoracic Disease. All rights reserved.
