TI  - Combining immunotherapy with radiation therapy in thoracic oncology.
PG  - S2492-S2507
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.05.73 [doi]
AB  - Thoracic malignancies comprise some of the most common and deadly cancers. 
      Immunotherapies have been proven to improve survival outcomes for patients with 
      advanced non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and show great potential for patients 
      with other thoracic malignancies. Radiation therapy (RT), an established and 
      effective treatment for thoracic cancers, has acted synergistically with 
      immunotherapies in preclinical studies. Ongoing clinical trials are exploring the 
      clinical benefits of combining RT with immunotherapies and the optimal manner in 
      which to deliver these complementary treatments.
