TI  - Subxiphoid approach for video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery: an update.
PG  - S1662-S1665
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.04.01 [doi]
AB  - The transthoracic video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) is considered as 
      standard operation for various thoracic diseases. With the development of 
      single-incision VATS, the thoracic surgery becomes less traumatic. However, 
      chronic chest wound pain still an issue despite the less invasive approach. 
      Therefore, subxiphoid VATS was proposed to overcome this problem. In this 
      article, we review current applications, pros and cons, and potential 
      developments of VATS through subxiphoid approach.
