DP  - 2018 May
TI  - Transcatheter aortic valve implantation for patients with lung cancer and aortic 
      valve stenosis.
PG  - E387-E390
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.04.83 [doi]
AB  - Many patients who require lung resection have cardiovascular and cerebrovascular 
      comorbidities. It has been recommended that surgical aortic valve replacement 
      (SAVR) should precede lung resection in patients with severe aortic valve 
      stenosis (AS). However, by first undergoing transcatheter aortic valve 
      implantation (TAVI), the patient may undergo lung resection more safely. We 
      present two patients with both severe AS and lung cancer who underwent TAVI and 
      lung resection without any complications.
