PMID- 29629203
OWN - NLM
STAT- PubMed-not-MEDLINE
LR  - 20220408
IS  - 2072-1439 (Print)
IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 10
IP  - Suppl 4
DP  - 2018 Mar
TI  - Enhanced recovery after surgery and video-assisted thoracic surgery lobectomy: 
      the Italian VATS Group surgical protocol.
PG  - S564-S570
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.01.157 [doi]
AB  - Enhanced recovery after surgery (ERAS(®)) is a strategy that seeks to reduce 
      patients' perioperative stress response, thereby reducing potential 
      complications, decreasing hospital length of stay and enabling patients to return 
      more quickly to their baseline functional status. The concept was introduced in 
      the late 1990s and was first adopted in patients undergoing open colorectal 
      surgery. Since then, the concept of ERAS has been adopted by multiple surgical 
      specialties. The diffusion of video-assisted thoracic surgery lobectomy (VATS-L) 
      sets also the surgical treatment of lung cancer as a new area for ERAS 
      development. In this paper, we present the Italian VATS Group (www.vatsgroup.org) 
      surgical protocol as part of the ERAS clinical pathway belonging to the VATS-L 
      national database.
