IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 10
IP  - 1
DP  - 2018 Jan
TI  - Intramedullary reinforcement of sternal fixation with autologous xiphoid tenon.
PG  - 472-475
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.12.63 [doi]
AB  - Minimally invasive cardiac surgery through a partial sternotomy or a 
      ministernotomy is popular. However, the transverse nonunion of the sternum will 
      be a potential complication. Valid and valuable techniques have been introduced 
      for securing the sternotomy fixation. Most of them are focused on the materials 
      or methods for extrinsic reinforcement. A new concept, focused on the 
      intramedullary reinforcement of the sternal fixation, was designed by 
      incarcerating a cancellous portion of the autologous xiphoid in the marrow space 
      of the inter-segmental junction of the partial sternotomy. This autologous 
      xiphoid tenon method is simple, reliable, and reproducible without additional 
      requirement of device implantation or an iliac incision for the bone grafting.
