TI  - Clinical update on central hypersomnias.
PG  - S112-S123
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.10.161 [doi]
AB  - The central hypersomnias encompass a range of conditions causing persisting or 
      intermittent excessive daytime sleepiness (EDS). These conditions therefore 
      present not infrequently in general clinical sleep practice, and remain in the 
      differential for patients presenting with sleepiness. Our understanding of the 
      pathophysiology, diagnosis and management of these conditions has progressed 
      significantly over recent years, and in this article we review this group of 
      disorders, focussing in particular on recent changes in classification and 
      diagnosis, pathophysiological advances, and novel treatment options.
