DP  - 2017 Dec
TI  - Post-transplant native pneumonectomy for interstitial fibrosis and small cell 
      lung cancer.
PG  - E1096-E1099
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.10.106 [doi]
AB  - Lung transplantation is a definitive treatment for select patients with end-stage 
      pulmonary disease. Following transplantation, the reported rate of lung cancer is 
      between 1-9% and is associated with a variety of risk factors, including smoking 
      history and chronic immunosuppression. The majority of post-transplant lung 
      cancer reported in the literature is histologically classified as non-small cell 
      lung carcinoma (NSCLC). We report a unique case of early stage small cell lung 
      carcinoma (SCLC) identified in the native lung following single lung 
      transplantation.
