VI  - 9
IP  - 9
DP  - 2017 Sep
TI  - Lung metastases in an atypical type A thymoma variant.
PG  - E805-E807
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.07.109 [doi]
AB  - A 35-year-old woman had undergone extensive thymothymectomy for type A thymoma 
      several years ago. However, two small lung nodules were found 4 and 5 years after 
      surgery. After a partial lung resection to remove these nodules, pathology 
      revealed that they were metastases of the type A thymoma. A pathological 
      re-evaluation confirmed that the primary tumor had in fact been an atypical type 
      A thymoma variant, a subset added to the WHO classification in 2015. Pathology 
      should be re-evaluated in all patients diagnosed with type A thymoma before 2015 
      since they may have the more aggressive atypical type A thymoma variant.
