TI  - Surgery for a large tracheoesophageal fistula using extracorporeal membrane 
      oxygenation.
PG  - E735-E738
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.03 [doi]
AB  - We report a patient with a giant tracheoesophageal fistula (TEF) planned for 
      reconstructive surgery. Because mechanical ventilation in any form was 
      technically impossible, we successfully used veno-venous extracorporeal membrane 
      oxygenation (VV-ECMO) without the need for mechanical ventilation.
