TI  - Four arm robotic-assisted pulmonary resection-right upper lobectomy: how to do 
      it.
PG  - 3302-3306
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.141 [doi]
AB  - Numerous published articles have shown the safety and efficacy of robotic lung 
      resection, including lobectomy. Several techniques have been described by 
      different authors to perform a robot assisted lung lobectomy. We adopted four 
      arms robotic procedure. We usually perform three ports (10-15 mm) and an anterior 
      3 to 4 cm utility incision. This technique allows to safely proceed with an 
      anterior to posterior approach to the hilum. In this study, we present in clear 
      and sequential steps, the procedure to perform a right upper lobectomy for early 
      stage lung cancer. We also supply a high-quality video, operative tips and a 
      preference cards.
