TI  - CT localization for a patient with a ground-glass opacity pulmonary nodule 
      expecting thoracoscopy: a mixture of lipiodol and India ink.
PG  - E349-E353
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.03.58 [doi]
AB  - Small and deeply seated pure ground-glass opacity (GGO) pulmonary nodules (PNs) 
      are not discernible during video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS). Moreover, 
      pathologists have difficulty in detecting these nodules due to insufficient 
      localization. We percutaneously injected a mixture of lipiodol and India ink 
      during preoperative CT-guided localization in a 52-year-old female patient 
      presenting with a pure GGO PN. A black-pigmented tattoo lesion was clearly 
      identified, and thoracoscopic wedge resection was performed without difficulty. 
      Pathologic results were also discernible, thus allowing the target lesion to be 
      identified without interruption for microscopic analysis. We introduce a novel 
      method using a mixture of lipiodol and India ink with satisfactory results for 
      preoperative localization of GGO PNs prior to VATS.
