TI  - Thoracoscopic management of incarcerated lung herniation after blunt chest 
      trauma: a case report and literature review.
PG  - E253-E257
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.03.41 [doi]
AB  - Traumatic lung herniation is a rare condition that is usually treated with 
      thoracotomy and pericostal fixation of adjacent ribs with sutures. We described a 
      traumatic lung herniation case successfully managed with hernia reduction and 
      double-layered repair of the intrathoracic defect, completed via a total 
      thoracoscopic approach.
