DP  - 2017 Mar
TI  - Primary tracheal schwannoma treated by surgical resection: a case report.
PG  - E249-E252
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.02.85 [doi]
AB  - The rarity and non-specific symptoms of benign primary tracheal tumors always 
      leaded to misdiagnosis and delayed treatment, and also undefined the optimal 
      treatment. In this case, a 45-year-old woman had a history of progressive 
      shortness of breath and dry cough for several years, CT scan revealed an 
      intra-luminal tracheal mass invaded the left side of tracheal wall. After being 
      located by bronchoscope preoperatively, the tumor was removed by surgical 
      resection. The tumor was 1.5 cm in diameter with intact capsule. The pathological 
      result confirmed the diagnosis of schwannoma.
