TI  - Tracheal and bronchial tumors.
PG  - 3781-3786
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.12.67 [doi]
AB  - Although primary tracheobronchial tumors are extremely rare in children, 
      recurrent respiratory symptoms resistant to conventional therapy require further 
      investigations to exclude possible malignant obstructive causes. As the matter of 
      fact, early diagnosis may allow minimally invasive surgeries, improving the 
      standard of living and the globally survival rate. The aim of this article is to 
      provide an overview of diagnosis and management of tracheobronchial tumors in the 
      early age, since only few reports are reported in the worldwide literature.
