TI  - Where do we go from here? Reappraising the data on anticoagulation in pulmonary 
      arterial hypertension.
PG  - E298-304
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.03.67 [doi]
AB  - The use of anticoagulation as part of the treatment regimen in pulmonary arterial 
      hypertension (PAH) remains a topic of debate. A recently published analysis of 
      anticoagulation use in the Registry to Evaluate Early and Long-Term PAH Disease 
      Management (REVEAL) study offers conflicting conclusions regarding the benefit of 
      this therapeutic strategy. There remains no robust randomized trial in PAH 
      weighing the risks versus benefits of including anticoagulation in treatment 
      regimens, leaving clinicians to surmise value in individual patients. 
      Reexamination of available data may help to provide guidance on this 
      controversial topic in the absence of future dedicated investigations.
