TI  - Routine use of preoperative breast MRI for patients considered for intraoperative 
      radiotherapy.
PG  - 765-8
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.03.27 [doi]
AB  - This editorial comments on the study by Tallet et al. which reported on the 
      incidence of ipsilateral second breast cancers (BC) detected by preoperative 
      magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) in patients being considered for intraoperative 
      radiotherapy (IORT). Any second BC was detected in 7% of patients; an ipsilateral 
      BC was detected in 4% of patients, precluding them from IORT. The authors comment 
      that in view of detection of a substantial rate of ipsilateral BCs by 
      preoperative MRI, this exam should be used routinely for staging patients being 
      considered for IORT.
