TI  - Remote preconditioning and cardiac surgery: regrouping after Remote Ischemic 
      Preconditioning for Heart Surgery (RIPHeart) and Effect of Remote Ischemic 
      Preconditioning on Clinical Outcomes in Patients Undergoing Coronary Artery 
      Bypass Surgery (ERICCA).
PG  - E197-9
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.01.81 [doi]
AB  - Remote ischaemic preconditioning (RIPC) is an attractive cardioprotective 
      strategy. Although results from animal studies and phase II study on humans are 
      convincing, it cannot have a role in clinical practice until benefits in clinical 
      outcomes are proven in phase III study. Two phase III studies were recently 
      published [Remote Ischemic Preconditioning for Heart Surgery (RIPHeart) and 
      Effect of Remote Ischemic Preconditioning on Clinical Outcomes in Patients 
      Undergoing Coronary Artery Bypass Surgery (ERICCA)] and this article discusses 
      their design, results and implications.
