DP  - 2016 Mar
TI  - Surgical anatomy of the tracheobronchial tree.
PG  - S121-9
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2016.01.69 [doi]
AB  - Airway surgery is often indicated in the management of benign or malignant 
      pathological processes of the tracheobronchial tree. The surgeon undertaking this 
      type of work has, however, the responsibility of understanding the particular 
      anatomy applicable to these structures and procedures as well as be able to 
      correlate imaging, intraoperative findings and anatomy. These are important 
      considerations if one wants to reduce operative morbidity and improve potential 
      for better long-term results. This paper reviews the most important anatomic 
      features of the tracheobronchial tree putting emphasis on those features that are 
      important to surgeons performing surgical procedures on those organs.
