TI  - Electromagnetic navigation bronchoscopy guided injection of methylene blue 
      combined with hookwire for preoperative localization of small pulmonary lesions 
      in thoracoscopic surgery.
PG  - E652-6
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.12.24 [doi]
AB  - Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) has been widely used in the resection 
      of small pulmonary lesions in the clinical practice. The accurate preoperative 
      localization of small pulmonary lesions is significant to guide the operation. We 
      report a thoracoscopic pulmonary wedge resection with electromagnetic navigation 
      bronchoscopy (ENB) guided injection of methylene blue combined with hookwire to 
      localize the small pulmonary lesion in a 50-year-old woman. We successfully 
      performed VATS followed by the combined localization of these two methods. This 
      localization method has a higher accuracy and fewer complications, which can 
      effectively guide the surgical resection.
