TI  - The future of left ventricular assist devices.
PG  - 2188-93
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.11.01 [doi]
AB  - The widespread acceptance of left ventricular assist device (LVAD) implantation 
      in the treatment of heart failure has revolutionized the way end stage heart 
      failure is treated. Advances in LVAD technology combined with a better 
      understanding of patient selection has led to unparalleled survival as well as a 
      reduction in the adverse event profile of these pumps. As our understanding of 
      heart failure continues to grow, there is little doubt that LVADs will continue 
      to play a pivotal role as a therapeutic option for those suffering from heart 
      failure.
