TI  - Bilateral multiple intrapulmonary nodules: a puzzled and rare disease.
PG  - E182-5
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.06.06 [doi]
AB  - Primary intrapulmonary spindle cell thymomas (PISCT) are rare lesions that may be 
      mistaken for a variety of benign and malignant epithelial or mesenchymal tumors. 
      It is thought as one subtype of primary intrapulmonary thymomas (PIT). To the 
      best of our knowledge, no bilateral multiple primary intrapulmonary spindle 
      thymomas and treatment had been reported in literature. We fortunately diagnosed 
      and managed this unique case, which might provide some experience for physicians 
      who were interested in this disease.
