TI  - The impact of percutaneous coronary intervention of chronic total occlusions on 
      left ventricular function and clinical outcomes.
PG  - 1107-10
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.07.24 [doi]
AB  - A meta-analysis by Hoebers et al. reported that successful chronic total 
      occlusion (CTO) recanalization resulted in an increase in left ventricular (LV) 
      ejection fraction by 4.44% (P<0.01) and a reduction in LV end-diastolic volume by 
      6.14 mL/m(2) during follow-up as compared with baseline, suggesting beneficial LV 
      remodeling. These findings are important as the myocardium supplied by a CTO 
      frequently has sustained irreversible injury and further support the clinical 
      benefits of CTO interventions.
