TI  - A large malignant thymomas of the anterior mediastinum.
PG  - E88-91
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.04.32 [doi]
AB  - The surgical treatment of large malignant thymomas of the anterior mediastinum is 
      associated with a high risk. Recently, a patient with a large malignant thymoma 
      of the anterior mediastinum was treated with surgery, and the outcome is 
      satisfactory. The diagnosis of such tumors is mostly based on the chest X-ray and 
      CT scans, as well as magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). Surgical treatment is the 
      main effective treatment, and should be performed as soon as possible.
