TI  - Surgical management of non-mycobacterial fungal infections.
PG  - S3398-S3407
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.08.85 [doi]
AB  - Fungal infections of the lung are common in endemic areas and in 
      immunocompromised patients. Antifungal therapy is the cornerstone of medical 
      therapy for most pulmonary fungi but surgery is an important adjunct in cases of 
      complicated disease or resistant organisms. A multidisciplinary approach 
      including pulmonary medicine, infectious disease, interventional radiology, and 
      thoracic surgery is favored. This article reviews the surgical management of 
      common fungal pulmonary infections and their sequelae.
