VI  - 10
IP  - Suppl 7
DP  - 2018 Apr
TI  - Liquid biopsy for early stage lung cancer.
PG  - S876-S881
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.04.26 [doi]
AB  - Liquid biopsy, which analyzes biological fluids especially blood specimen to 
      detect and quantify circulating cancer biomarkers, have been rapidly introduced 
      and represents a promising potency in clinical practice of lung cancer diagnosis 
      and prognosis. Unlike conventional tissue biopsy, liquid biopsy is non-invasive, 
      safe, simple in procedure, and is not influenced by manipulators' skills. 
      Notably, some circulating cancer biomarkers are already detectable in disease 
      with low-burden, making liquid biopsy feasible in detecting early stage lung 
      cancer. In this review, we described a landscape of different liquid biopsy 
      methods by highlighting the rationale and advantages, accessing the value of 
      various circulating biomarkers and discussing their possible future development 
      in the detection of early lung cancer.
