TI  - Disseminated intravascular coagulopathy caused by type II endoleak after 
      endovascular aneurysm repair in severe aortic stenosis.
PG  - E994-E996
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.10.49 [doi]
AB  - A 72-year-old man with severe aortic stenosis (AS) presented with a type II 
      endoleak after endovascular aneurysm repair (EVAR). Laboratory findings were 
      consistent with disseminated intravascular coagulopathy (DIC) with 
      thrombocytopenia. The platelet count increased slightly after aortic valve 
      replacement but fully recovered with the reversal of DIC after surgical repair of 
      the type II endoleak.
