TI  - Bridging to lung transplantation with extracorporeal circulatory support: when or 
      when not?
PG  - 3352-3361
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.117 [doi]
AB  - Patients with end-stage lung disease who are candidates for lung transplantation 
      may acutely decompensate before a donor organ becomes available. In this 
      scenario, extracorporeal life support (ECLS) may be considered as a bridge to 
      transplant or as a bridge to decision. In the current chapter, we review the 
      indications, techniques, and outcomes for bridging to lung transplantation with 
      ECLS.
