PMID- 29214066
OWN - NLM
STAT- PubMed-not-MEDLINE
LR  - 20220318
IS  - 2072-1439 (Print)
IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 9
IP  - Suppl 10
DP  - 2017 Sep
TI  - A systematic approach to the management of massive hemoptysis.
PG  - S1069-S1086
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.06.41 [doi]
AB  - Massive hemoptysis is regarded as a potentially lethal condition that requires 
      immediate attention, and prompt action. Although minor hemoptysis is frequently 
      encountered by most clinicians, massive hemoptysis in far less frequent and most 
      physicians are not prepared to manage this time-sensitive clinical presentation 
      in a systematic and timely fashion. Critical initial steps in management need to 
      be implemented in an expedited fashion, such that patients may have a chance at a 
      more definitive treatment. In this article, we review the definition, vascular 
      anatomy, etiology, diagnostic evaluation, epidemiology and prognostic markers of 
      massive hemoptysis. A systematic approach to management, stabilization and 
      treatment options is followed. An algorithm is proposed for the management of 
      massive hemoptysis and the importance of a multidisciplinary approach is 
      emphasized.
