TI  - Single-stage surgery experience in a case of coarctation of the aorta with an 
      arch aneurysm combined with severe coronary artery disease.
PG  - E714-E717
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.07.41 [doi]
AB  - The best surgical approach for coarctation of the aorta (COA) combined with other 
      cardiac diseases is uncertain. The simultaneous intracardiac repair of complex 
      pathologies is desirable because multistage procedures may lead to a higher rate 
      of mortality. We describe a case involving a 61-year-old woman who was suffering 
      from COA with a concomitant arch aneurysm and coronary artery disease. We managed 
      her case via single-stage surgery that included a median sternotomy.
