TI  - Single lung retrieval from a donor supported by a left ventricular assist device.
PG  - E685-E688
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.07.09 [doi]
AB  - The number of patients who need cardiac support with a left ventricular assist 
      device (LVAD) has increased over the last decade. However, the number of reports 
      of organ retrieval from donors with an LVAD is still small. Successful lung 
      retrieval for single lung transplantation was performed from a donor on LVAD 
      support. This required special care not to injure the heart, great vessels, and 
      the device, particularly the outflow conduit, because of significant 
      conglutination around the device. A right single lung transplantation was 
      performed successfully, with no postoperative complications. This means that 
      patients on an LVAD could be potential donors for lung transplantation.
