TI  - Two cases of pulmonary cysticercosis manifesting as pleural effusion: case report 
      and literature review.
PG  - E677-E681
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.07.04 [doi]
AB  - Cysticercosis is an important public health problem in developing countries. The 
      major involvement sites are the central nervous system and the eyes, although 
      striated muscles and subcutaneous tissues are frequently involved in the 
      disseminated form of disease. Pulmonary involvement in cysticercosis is very rare 
      and ill-defined nodular shadows distributed throughout the lung is the usual 
      radiological presentation. Only one case of cysticercosis presenting as lung 
      cavity with pleural effusion has been reported so far in literature. We describe 
      two cases in which pleural effusion due to cysticercosis were detected on chest 
      X-ray and computed tomography (CT) scan.
