TI  - How to describe univariate data.
PG  - 1741-1743
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.05.80 [doi]
AB  - Univariate analysis has the purpose to describe a single variable distribution in 
      one sample. It is the first important step of every clinical trial. In this short 
      review, we focus on this analysis, the methods that authors should use to report 
      this type of data, information that they should not miss and mistakes that they 
      must avoid.
