DP  - 2017 Jun
TI  - Pediatric airway surgery.
PG  - 1663-1671
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.05.50 [doi]
AB  - The management of pediatric airway pathology can be challenging and requires a 
      dedicated team, consisting of thoracic surgeons, phoniatricians, logopedics, 
      pediatricians and anesthetists. It necessitates a tailored treatment approach for 
      each individual patient in order to address the minor variances that exist 
      between cases. The majority of pediatric airway problems are a sequela of 
      prematurity and prolonged post-partal intubation/tracheostomy. Surgical repair is 
      often complicated by additional malformation or severe comorbidities. This 
      comprehensive review should give an overview on most common airway problems in 
      neonates and children as well as available surgical techniques.
