TI  - CT angio for the evaluation of graft patency.
PG  - S283-S288
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.03.111 [doi]
AB  - Invasive coronary angiography (ICA) is the traditional method for the follow-up 
      of graft patency in coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) patients. Nevertheless, 
      the advent of multidetector computed tomography (MDCT) opened new perspectives 
      for using a noninvasive, equally reliable method to study CABG patients. This 
      review article will analyze the current feasibility of modern multi-slice MDCT, 
      as well as its future perspectives.
