DP  - 2017 Apr
TI  - Serendipity and innovation: history and evolution of transthoracic 
      echocardiography.
PG  - S257-S263
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.03.90 [doi]
AB  - The history of echocardiography is sprinkled with many interesting episodes and 
      anecdotes showing that devoting your life to the pursuit of one goal is 
      praiseworthy, and that at the same time, a little luck goes a long way. 
      Transthoracic echocardiography (TTE) has led to dramatic improvements in 
      cardiovascular medicine, and is now the most widely used diagnostic cardiac test 
      after electrocardiography (ECG). The present review pays tribute to the 
      pioneering efforts of those who believed in this innovative technology despite 
      mounted skepticism and briefly describes the evolution of TTE from its early days 
      to the most recent developments.
