TI  - Delayed-onset tension hemothorax following blunt trauma and the rupture of a 
      previously undiagnosed aberrant right subclavian artery.
PG  - E245-E248
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.02.87 [doi]
AB  - An arteria lusoria is a well-known anatomic variant of the right subclavian 
      artery. We describe a patient in whom an arteria lusoria injury was revealed by 
      delayed-onset tension hemothorax following blunt trauma to the thorax.
