TI  - Protective effect of angulated aorta for saving coronary artery during 
      endovascular repair for ascending aortic pseudoaneurysm.
PG  - E667-71
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.05.62 [doi]
AB  - Ascending aortic pseudoaneurysm is a rare complication after cardiothoracic 
      surgery and the open surgical repair for this complication is challenging. We 
      report on a patient who developed an ascending aortic pseudoaneurysm after aortic 
      valve replacement (AVR), which was treated successfully with endovascular 
      therapy. Our case showed that angulation of the ascending aorta is one of factors 
      for consideration in application of endovascular therapy and endovascular therapy 
      might be an option for management of ascending aortic pathology in patients with 
      high surgical risk, particularly patients with a severely angulated proximal 
      ascending aorta.
