DP  - 2016 Aug
TI  - Left ventricular assist devices-current state and perspectives.
PG  - E660-6
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.07.13 [doi]
AB  - Mechanical circulatory support devices have become an important treatment tool 
      for severe acute and chronic heart failure, since heart transplantation cannot 
      meet the demands because of a lack of available donor organs. Since implantation 
      of the first ventricular assist device a constant development of the suitability 
      of these devices has been made. This review will introduce different generations 
      of left ventricular assist devices (LVAD) and elaborate on clinical indications, 
      risk stratification and current literature.
