TI  - Chronic outpatient management of patients with a left ventricular assist device.
PG  - 2112-24
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.10.28 [doi]
AB  - The use of mechanical circulatory support (MCS) as treatment for advanced heart 
      failure (HF) has grown exponentially over the past 15 years. The continuous flow 
      left ventricular assist device (CF-LVAD) has become the most used form of MCS in 
      advanced HF, especially since approval of use as destination therapy (DT) and 
      with the lack of organ availability. Long-term survival has improved and diligent 
      outpatient management is thus particularly critical to achieve optimal outcomes. 
      This review will discuss outpatient management strategies for patients with HF 
      and a left ventricular assist device (LVAD).
