TI  - Thoracoscopic anatomical resection of congenital lung malformations in adults.
PG  - 486-9
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.01.50 [doi]
AB  - Congenital lung malformations (CLM) are a heterogeneous group of disorders that 
      may require surgical resection to prevent complications. Thoracoscopic resection 
      of CLM has been reported in infants. Our goal was to state whether it can also be 
      a viable option in adults. Between 2007 and 2014, 11 patients had a thoracoscopic 
      resection of a CLM (six lobectomies and five anatomic segmentectomies) with 
      satisfactory results. Although being more challenging in adults due to infectious 
      sequellae, this approach is safe.
