IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 7
IP  - 2
DP  - 2015 Feb
TI  - Surgical options in atrial fibrillation.
PG  - 204-13
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.12.34 [doi]
AB  - Atrial fibrillation (AF) is not benign and its prevalence is increasing. The two 
      main goals in management of atrial fibrillation are to optimize hemodynamics 
      through rate or rhythm control and to prevent systemic thrombo-embolism. To date, 
      these two goals are still sub-optimally achieved, raising the need for 
      alternative methods and strategies both pharmacologically and through 
      interventions. In this review, we discuss surgical strategies of achieving both 
      goals with insights on the evolution and potential future of these strategies.
