TI  - Left atrial appendage closure for thromboembolism prevention in patients with 
      atrial fibrillation: advances and perspectives.
PG  - 199-203
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.01.20 [doi]
AB  - Atrial fibrillation (AF) is a frequent cause of stroke. More than 90% of thrombi 
      were found in the left atrial appendage (LAA) in non-valvular AF. Transcatheter 
      LAA closure has been developed as a novel approach to reduce the risk of stroke 
      in patients with AF over the last decade. In this article, we review the recent 
      advances and propose the possible challenges regarding the LAA closure for 
      thromboembolism prevention in patients with AF.
