DP  - 2018 Nov
TI  - Cerebral embolic protection devices during transcatheter aortic valve 
      implantation: clinical versus silent embolism.
PG  - S3604-S3613
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.09.62 [doi]
AB  - Cerebrovascular events following transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) 
      is one of the most devastating complications. Several studies with magnetic 
      resonance or cerebral filters have demonstrated the universal brain embolization 
      after TAVI, in the majority of patients clinically silent. Embolic protection 
      devices (EPD) have been developed as a mechanical barrier to prevent these emboli 
      to reach cerebral vasculature and potentially reduce neurological events. We 
      review the current evidence about EPD in relation to histopathological and 
      cerebral imaging findings and neurological events.
