TI  - Bronchoscopic advances in the management of aerodigestive fistulas.
PG  - 5636-5647
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.05.44 [doi]
AB  - Malignant aerodigestive fistula (ADF) is an uncommon condition complicating 
      thoracic malignancies. It results in increased morbidity and mortality and 
      warrants therapeutic intervention. The management approach depends on symptoms, 
      configuration, location, and extent of the fistula. This article will discuss the 
      therapeutic considerations in the management of ADF.
