PMID- 30069383
OWN - NLM
STAT- PubMed-not-MEDLINE
LR  - 20201001
IS  - 2072-1439 (Print)
IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 10
IP  - 6
DP  - 2018 Jun
TI  - Computed tomography-guided localization with laser angle guide for thoracic 
      procedures.
PG  - 3824-3828
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.05.162 [doi]
AB  - Computed tomography (CT)-guided lung procedures such as preoperative 
      localizations, biopsies, and ablations are associated with morbidity even 
      mortality. Often, the puncture angle is determined by the 'experienced hand' 
      without a precise guide. We describe here the Laser Angle Guide Assembly(®) to 
      direct and steer the puncture angles precisely. It decreases procedure-related 
      complications, saves time, reduces costs, avoids repeated punctures, and 
      minimizes radiation exposures.
