TI  - Novel techniques for video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery segmentectomy.
PG  - S1671-S1676
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.05.207 [doi]
AB  - Small lung cancers are being increasing diagnosed because of advances in computed 
      tomography (CT) and low-dose CT screening. Sublobar resection of peripheral, 
      small lung nodules, such as ground-glass nodules, is a useful therapeutic option 
      that obtains both a pathological diagnosis and radical cure. Lung segmentectomy 
      is a better option than wedge resection for securing a sufficient surgical margin 
      and can also be used to assess hilar nodes. Anatomical segmentectomy, however, is 
      a technically more complicated operative procedure than standard lobectomy. We 
      describe the issues and novel techniques of video-assisted thoracoscopic 
      segmentectomy.
