TI  - Thoracoscopic lobectomy for massive hemoptysis caused by complete pulmonary vein 
      occlusion after radiofrequency ablation for atrial fibrillation.
PG  - E296-E300
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.03.164 [doi]
AB  - Complete pulmonary vein occlusion is a rare complication of transcatheter 
      radiofrequency ablation for atrial fibrillation. We here report a 37-year-old man 
      who presented with massive hemoptysis as a result of left superior pulmonary vein 
      occlusion caused by transcatheter radiofrequency ablation for paroxysmal atrial 
      fibrillation. The patient was successfully managed with thoracoscopic left upper 
      lobectomy with a satisfactory outcome.
