TI  - Aorta-atria-septum combined incision for aortic valve re-replacement.
PG  - E285-E288
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.04.48 [doi]
AB  - This case report illustrates a patient who underwent supra-annular mechanical 
      aortic valve replacement then suffered from prosthesis dysfunction, increasing 
      pressure gradient with aortic valve. She was successfully underwent aortic valve 
      re-replacement, sub-annular pannus removing and aortic annulus enlargement 
      procedures through combined cardiac incision passing through aortic root, right 
      atrium (RA), and upper atrial septum. This incision provides optimal visual 
      operative field and simplifies dissection.
