PMID- 29707370
OWN - NLM
STAT- PubMed-not-MEDLINE
LR  - 20200930
IS  - 2072-1439 (Print)
IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 10
IP  - 3
DP  - 2018 Mar
TI  - Successful repair of neonatal tricuspid regurgitation due to chordae rupture.
PG  - E186-E188
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.02.08 [doi]
AB  - Neonatal rupture of the chordae of tricuspid valve with severe regurgitation is 
      rare and disastrous. We report on a full-term female neonate presented with 
      cyanosis caused by severe tricuspid regurgitation (TR) due to anterior leaflet 
      chordal rupture. After initial stabilization by prostaglandin E1 infusion, 
      successful early repair was achieved with artificial chordae implantation. The 
      unique pathophysiology and the therapeutic strategy of this situation will be 
      described.
