TI  - Metastatic small bowel neuroendocrine tumour and carcinoid heart disease with 
      aortic valve involvement-a rare occurrence.
PG  - E103-E107
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.01.52 [doi]
AB  - Carcinoid disease of the heart commonly affects the tricuspid and pulmonary 
      valves causing thickening and stenosis. However in very rare circumstances, the 
      disease can also involve the mitral and aortic valves. We present an unusual case 
      of left sided carcinoid heart disease (CHD) and triple valve replacement without 
      the presence of proven intra-cardiac shunts or bronchial carcinoid lesions.
