TI  - Symptomatic sinus arrest induced by acute marijuana use.
PG  - 1121-1123
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.01.139 [doi]
AB  - Marijuana is considered a drug of low-toxicity, however its chronic and excessive 
      use is regarded as a risk factor for general and cardiovascular health. Although 
      investigated for therapeutic benefits, it can evoke electrocardiographic 
      abnormalities in a dose-dependent manner. We report a case of a 54-year-old 
      female who presented to the emergency department (ED) experiencing intermittent 
      episodes of presyncope with tingling sensations around the left-side of the mouth 
      and arm following acute inhalation of marijuana. Documented episodes of sinus 
      arrest were noted.
