TI  - Emergency drain for post pneumonectomy bronchopleural fistula: a drain placement 
      technique based on the siphon principle.
PG  - 468-471
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.11.145 [doi]
AB  - Post pneumonectomy bronchopleural fistula (BPF) is a life-threatening 
      complication requiring pleural cavity drainage to avoid acute mediastinal shift 
      and contralateral aspiration pneumonia. Chest drain insertion in this situation 
      may be technically difficult because of drastic anatomical changes such as 
      mediastinal dislocation, diaphragm elevation and, sometimes, massive subcutaneous 
      emphysema. In addition, the most important part of the pleural cavity to be 
      drained is the costophrenic recess that is scarcely drained by a standard chest 
      tube with its tip aiming high and upwards. We propose a safe, simple and 
      effective technique based on the siphon principle to drain the lowest part of the 
      pleural cavity.
