DP  - 2017 Nov
TI  - One-stage surgery in combination with thoracic endovascular grafting and 
      resection of T4 lung cancer invading the thoracic aorta and spine.
PG  - E1009-E1012
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.10.101 [doi]
AB  - A novel strategy of one-stage surgery in combination with thoracic endovascular 
      grafting and resection for T4 lung cancer invading the thoracic aorta and spine 
      is described. A 56-year-old man with locally advanced lung cancer infiltrating 
      the aortic wall and spine underwent neoadjuvant chemotherapy and thoracic 
      irradiation, followed by en bloc resection of the aortic wall and spine with 
      thoracic endovascular grafting. He developed postoperative chylothorax, but there 
      were no stent graft-related events. After 3 months, computed tomography (CT) did 
      not show aortic stent graft stenosis, migration, or deformation.
