TI  - Uniportal video-assisted lobectomy through a posterior approach.
PG  - 4057-4063
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.09.87 [doi]
AB  - We propose a technique of uniportal VATS lobectomy using a posterior approach. 
      The main differences of our technique versus standard anterior uniportal VATS are 
      the following: (I) the surgical incision is performed in the auscultatory 
      triangle instead of in the posterior axillary line and (II) the surgeon is placed 
      posteriorly to the patient rather than anteriorly. For thoracic surgeons who are 
      familiar with posterolateral thoracotomy, our technique allows to replicate the 
      same maneuvers performed in the open approach. This strategy was applied with 
      success in 19 consecutive patients for anatomical resection of neoplastic (n=17) 
      and benign (n=2) diseases.
