DP  - 2017 Sep
TI  - Thoracoscopic left S4a subsegmentectomy.
PG  - 3299-3301
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.07.64 [doi]
AB  - A 63-year-old woman who underwent a left hepatic lobectomy for hilar 
      cholangiocarcinoma was referred to our department for further management. Chest 
      computed tomography showed a lung nodule that was increased in size to 8 mm in 
      the S4a. The differential diagnosis was metastasis versus primary lung cancer. 
      Thoracoscopic left S4a subsegmentectomy was performed. The operative time was 158 
      min. The blood loss was minimal. Air leakage was not observed, and a chest tube 
      was removed on POD 1. The patient was discharged home on POD 3. The final 
      diagnosis was primary lung cancer (T1aN0M0 stage IA). Surgical margin was 2.0 cm.
