TI  - Types of biological variables.
PG  - 1730-1733
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.05.75 [doi]
AB  - Identification and description of variables used in any study is a necessary 
      component in biomedical research. Statistical analyses rely on the type of 
      variables that are involved in the study. In this short article, we introduce the 
      different types of biological variables. A researcher has to be familiar with the 
      type of variable he/she is dealing with in his/her research to decide about 
      appropriate graphs/diagrams, summary measures and statistical analysis.
