TI  - Imaging-guided thoracoscopic resection of a ground-glass opacity lesion in a 
      hybrid operating room equipped with a robotic C-arm CT system.
PG  - E416-E419
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.04.48 [doi]
AB  - The intraoperative identification of small pulmonary nodules through 
      video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery remains challenging. Although preoperative 
      CT-guided nodule localization is commonly used to detect tumors during 
      video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS), this approach carries inherent 
      risks. We report the case of a patient with stage I lung cancer presenting as an 
      area of ground-glass opacity (GGO) in the right upper pulmonary lobe. He 
      successfully underwent a single-stage, CT-guided localization and removal of the 
      pulmonary nodule within a hybrid operating room (OR) equipped with a robotic 
      C-arm.
