TI  - Sublobar resection for stage IA non-small cell lung cancer.
PG  - S208-S210
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.03.135 [doi]
AB  - Advancements in the diagnosis, staging and management of lung cancer have all led 
      to improvements in outcomes associated with sublobar resection. Lobectomy, for 
      early stage lung cancers has been the treatment of choice for many years. 
      However, there is mounting evidence that sublobar resection when applied to the 
      appropriate patient population can provide not only excellent oncologic results 
      but also equivalent survival to lobectomy. Therefore, it is time that we 
      reevaluate the management of peripheral stage IA lung cancers.
