TI  - Chronic pulmonary mucormycosis: an emerging fungal infection in diabetes 
      mellitus.
PG  - E121-E125
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.02.31 [doi]
AB  - Mucormycosis commonly affects immunocompromised individuals with defects in 
      neutrophil function or count. Diabetes mellitus is an important risk factor due 
      to impair innate and acquired immunity for mucormycosis, with 
      rhino-orbital-cerebral involvement as a common presentation. Pulmonary 
      mucormycosis (PM) although a rare presentation in diabetic patients but is 
      associated with high mortality and morbidity. An early diagnosis of PM is 
      difficult, due to rarity of the disease and clinical and radiological features 
      resembling tuberculosis (TB) which is common in Pakistan. Here we present three 
      cases of chronic PM in patients with diabetes and with no other apparent risk 
      factors.
