TI  - Update on the diagnosis and treatment of tracheal and bronchial injury.
PG  - E50-E56
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.01.19 [doi]
AB  - Tracheal and bronchial injury, including iatrogenic injury and traumatic injury, 
      the former usually occurred in the operation, intubation or bronchoscopy. The 
      latter was occurred in a variety of blunt trauma, often combined with a variety 
      of complex injuries. The therapeutic approach can be differentiated, surgical or 
      conservative, no criteria has been universally accepted. Successful treatment of 
      tracheobronchial injuries requires early diagnostic evaluation. This article aims 
      to review the indications and therapeutic options for tracheal and bronchial 
      injuries.
