PMID- 28149579
OWN - NLM
STAT- PubMed-not-MEDLINE
LR  - 20220321
IS  - 2072-1439 (Print)
IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 8
IP  - 12
DP  - 2016 Dec
TI  - Endobronchial tuberculosis-a review.
PG  - 3797-3802
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.12.73 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial tuberculosis (EBTB) is a tuberculous infection of the 
      tracheobronchial tree with microbial and histopathological evidence. Patients may 
      present with symptoms secondary to disease itself or from the complication of 
      disease like endobronchial obstruction. Diagnosis requires a high index of 
      suspicion. Computed tomography (CT) and bronchoscopy along with microbiological 
      investigations are the most useful diagnostic tools for the confirmation as well 
      as for the evaluation of the tracheobronchial stenosis. The goals of treatment 
      are eradication of tubercle bacilli with anti-tubercular medications and the 
      prevention of airway stenosis. Interventional Bronchoscopic techniques and 
      surgery is required for those patients who develop severe tracheobronchial 
      stenosis that causing significant symptoms including dyspnea, repeated post 
      obstructive pneumonia or bronchiectasis.
