PMID- 27942411
OWN - NLM
STAT- PubMed-not-MEDLINE
LR  - 20220316
IS  - 2072-1439 (Print)
IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 8
IP  - Suppl 11
DP  - 2016 Nov
TI  - Surgery for lung cancer invading the mediastinum.
PG  - S889-S894
AB  - Lung cancer infiltrating the mediastinum is a subset of locally advanced lung 
      tumors for which surgery is not routinely offered. Radical operations that 
      involve removal of adjacent mediastinal structures to obtain free margins may 
      provide a realistic cure. Such extended resections are typically reserved to 
      highly motivated patients seeking more aggressive management, and are only 
      offered following complete evaluation on a case-by-case basis. Positive prognosis 
      depends on complete R0 resection and lack of mediastinal nodal metastases. 
      Careful and exhaustive preoperative planning as well as surgical expertise cannot 
      be overemphasized for successful surgical outcomes. Here we provide a brief 
      summary of the literature as well as our own experience managing these rare and 
      sometimes challenging surgeries.
