TI  - P value interpretations and considerations.
PG  - E928-E931
AB  - Application and interpretation of statistical evaluation of relationships is a 
      necessary element in biomedical research. Statistical analyses rely on P value to 
      demonstrate relationships. The traditional level of significance, P<0.05, can be 
      negatively impacted by small sample size, bias, and random error, and has evolved 
      to include interpretation of statistical trends, correction factors for multiple 
      analyses, and acceptance of statistical significance for P>0.05 for complex 
      relationships such as effect modification.
