TI  - Non-intubated laparoscopic repair of giant Morgagni's hernia for a young man.
PG  - E698-701
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.07.87 [doi]
AB  - An asymptomatic patient was admitted as his chest photograph and computed 
      tomography scans showed a giant Morgagni's hernia (MH). And it was repaired by 
      laparoscopic approach under epidural anesthesia without endotracheal intubation. 
      The hernia content of omentum was repositioned back into the abdominal cavity, 
      and the diaphragmatic defect was repaired with composite mesh. Which indicated 
      that non-intubated laparoscopic mesh repair via epidural anesthesia is reliable 
      and satisfactory for MH.
