TI  - Non-intubated resection and reconstruction of trachea for the treatment of a mass 
      in the upper trachea.
PG  - 594-9
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.01.56 [doi]
AB  - Tumors of the upper trachea are typically treated by tracheal resection and 
      reconstruction via neck incision under general anesthesia. In recent years, 
      non-intubated thoracic surgery has been widely applied for the treatment of lung 
      diseases due to its advantages including quick postoperative recovery. In this 
      article, we describe the application of non-intubated tracheal resection and 
      reconstruction in one patient for the treatment of a mass in upper trachea.
