TI  - Clinical pathway for thoracic surgery in the United States.
PG  - S29-36
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.11.21 [doi]
AB  - The paradigm for postoperative care for thoracic surgical patients in the United 
      States has shifted with efforts to reduce hospital length of stay and improve 
      quality of life. The increasing usage of minimally invasive techniques in 
      thoracic surgery has been an important part of this. In this review we will 
      examine our standard practices as well as the evidence behind both general 
      contemporary postoperative care principles and those specific to certain 
      operations.
