TI  - Progress in the impact of polluted meteorological conditions on the incidence of 
      asthma.
PG  - E57-61
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.12.64 [doi]
AB  - It has been revealed by many studies that air pollution is one of the important 
      inducements of asthma exacerbations. In addition, meteorological conditions such 
      as high atmospheric pressure, low temperature, low humidity and large diurnal 
      amplitude can directly induce asthma. Meanwhile, meteorological conditions play 
      an important role in the diffusion, dilution and accumulation of air pollution. 
      This article reviewed research progress in the impact of polluted meteorological 
      conditions on the incidence of asthma.
