TI  - Recurrent infarctions due to a dome-shaped pannus above the mitral valve 
      prosthesis.
PG  - E130-2
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2016.01.29 [doi]
AB  - This report describes a unique case of a 56-year-old female who suffered from 
      recurrent stroke after double mechanical valve replacement. During the four years 
      after the surgery, she remained in normal sinus rhythm, received adequate 
      anticoagulation therapy, and no apparent left atrial thrombus was detected. She 
      underwent redo surgery to prevent further stroke after fourth instance of 
      cerebral infarction. Intraoperative findings revealed a 'dome-shaped' pannus 
      formation covering the sewing ring of the mitral prosthesis circumferentially, 
      probably leading to clot formation and repeated infarctions. She has been stroke 
      free for three years after pannus resection.
