TI  - A novel sutureless technique for the repair of coronary sinus injuries.
PG  - 2359-61
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.12.43 [doi]
AB  - Coronary Sinus injury related to cardioplegia catheter insertion is a rare 
      complication associated with significant morbidity and mortality risk. We 
      describe a simple, safe and effective sutureless technique for the management of 
      coronary sinus injury. This technique was developed in a porcine haemostatic 
      workshop in Hamburg, Germany.
