TI  - A case of recurrent pneumothorax related to oral methylphenidate.
PG  - E255-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.07.36 [doi]
AB  - Primary spontaneous pneumothorax (PSP) commonly occurs in young, tall, and thin 
      males, without any identifiable cause except for emphysema-like changes (ELCs). 
      However, other risk factors may be overlooked. Herein, we report the case of a 
      19-year-old male who presented with recurrent spontaneous pneumothorax while 
      taking oral methylphenidate.
