TI  - Management of subsolid pulmonary nodules in CT lung cancer screening.
PG  - 1103-6
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.07.23 [doi]
AB  - The distinct appearance and behavior of subsolid pulmonary nodules (SSNs) has 
      resulted in separate recommendations for the management of solitary SSNs, both 
      for incidentally detected as well as for screen detected nodules. However, these 
      guidelines have been based primarily on expert opinion. Recently two studies were 
      published regarding SSNs detected in low-dose computed tomography (LDCT) lung 
      cancer screening, including management advices.
