TI  - Bronchial involvement in chronic eosinophilic pneumonia: a case report.
PG  - E97-E101
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.12.16 [doi]
AB  - Chronic eosinophilic pneumonia (CEP) is an idiopathic chronic condition 
      characterized by alveolar filling with mixed inflammatory infiltrate consisting 
      largely of eosinophils. On CT, it is usually observed as consolidation, often 
      peripheral and patchy in distribution, with upper lobe dominance. Airway 
      involvement in CEP is very rare. We report on a case of bronchial involvement in 
      CEP.
