PMID- 25713735
OWN - NLM
STAT- PubMed-not-MEDLINE
DCOM- 20150225
LR  - 20201001
IS  - 2072-1439 (Print)
IS  - 2077-6624 (Electronic)
IS  - 2072-1439 (Linking)
VI  - 7
IP  - 2
DP  - 2015 Feb
TI  - Alternative medicine in atrial fibrillation treatment-Yoga, acupuncture, 
      biofeedback and more.
PG  - 185-92
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.01.13 [doi]
AB  - The last decade has seen a significant improvement in the management of atrial 
      fibrillation (AF) with the development of newer medications and improvement in 
      catheter ablation techniques. Recurrence of AF remains a significant problem in 
      these patients and medications offer limited supportive role. Complementary and 
      alternative treatment strategies therefore remain a viable option for these AF 
      patients. Several studies have shown improvement in AF symptoms with yoga 
      therapy, acupuncture and biofeedback. There are also several herbal medicine and 
      supplements such as omega-3 fatty acids, antioxidant vitamins, barberry, 
      motherwort, cinchona, Shensongyangxin, hawthorn, Kella and Wenxin Keli that have 
      been evaluated as potential therapeutic options in AF. These studies are however 
      limited by small sample sizes with mixed results. Besides the pharmacological 
      action, metabolism, interactions with other medications and the adverse effects 
      of the herbal medications and supplements remain poorly understood. In spite of 
      the above limitations, complementary therapies remain a promising option in the 
      management of AF and further studies are necessary to validate their safety and 
      efficacy.
