TI  - Minimally invasive mesoesophageal resection.
PG  - S728-S734
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.12.39 [doi]
AB  - Based in the anatomical concept of the mesoesophagus, that at subcarinal level 
      all the vessels come through a by-layer connective tissue plane from the aorta to 
      the esophagus whereas supracarinally these structures will come from both sides, 
      with vagal and recurrent laryngeal nerves, a minimally invasive mesoesophageal 
      (MIME) resection model may be described. Based on this surgical plane concept, 
      dissection of esophagus and mediastinal lymphadenectomy can be performed along 
      these structures establishing clear anatomical modules for an adequate 
      oncological resection.
