DP  - 2019 Feb
TI  - Management of traumatic esophageal injuries.
PG  - S172-S176
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.10.86 [doi]
AB  - Traumatic esophageal perforations are rare but difficult to treat injuries. We 
      review the principles of work-up, anatomy and treatment of cervical, thoracic and 
      abdominal traumatic esophageal perforations. Management is dictated by location 
      of the perforation and any concurrent injuries. The majority of cases are 
      amenable to primary repair with flap re-enforcement. Other principles include 
      adequate drainage around the repair, decompression of the esophagus and stomach 
      (via nasogastric tube or gastrostomy tube) and distal enteral nutrition (feeding 
      jejunostomy).
