AB  - The medical management of bronchiectasis includes confirming the diagnosis of the 
      disease, evaluating the patient for possible underlying etiologies and then 
      properly assessing the patient for appropriate therapies. Patients with 
      bronchiectasis are heterogeneous and a personalized approach to each patient is 
      needed in order to properly formulate an optimal management plan.
