TI  - Operation for an anomalous systemic arterial supply to the left lower lobe using 
      an anastomosis procedure in an infant.
PG  - E301-E303
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.04.05 [doi]
AB  - An anomalous systemic arterial supply to a normal lung is a rare congenital 
      anomaly, and then for which no standard treatment has been established. We 
      present the case of a 7-month-old girl who had a continuous murmur at the trunk. 
      She was diagnosed the anomalous systemic arterial supply to the left lower lobe, 
      we decided to perform an end-to-side anastomosis between the abnormal systemic 
      artery and left pulmonary artery. After 3 years, the patient showed the normal 
      lung perfusion of the operation lobe.
