DP  - 2018 Apr
TI  - Electromagnetic navigation bronchoscopy under intravenous sedation-tips and 
      tricks.
PG  - S769-S774
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.03.98 [doi]
AB  - Electromagnetic navigation bronchoscopy (ENB) is gaining acceptance and 
      popularity amongst bronchoscopists as one of the tools to diagnose pulmonary 
      nodules (PNs). Although the majority of ENBs in earlier studies were performed 
      under general anaesthesia (GA), later reports suggest that the diagnostic yield 
      of ENB under intravenous sedation (IVS) was comparable, and was time saving. ENB 
      under IVS may potentially improve access of the techniques to practitioners and 
      patients. However, it is technically challenging when compared to its performance 
      under GA. This article reviews the techniques required for ENB under IVS to 
      maximize its diagnostic yield and safety.
