TI  - Urokinase application for hemothorax in pulmonary mucormycosis.
PG  - E175-E178
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.03.01 [doi]
AB  - We present an exemplary case of an immunocompromised patient with pulmonary 
      mucormycosis successfully treated by a combination of surgical removal of the 
      mucor and urokinase to control the recurring hemothorax. The use of urokinase in 
      hemothoraces is a way to reduce repetitive surgeries in weak patients.
