TI  - How to recognize silent atrial fibrillation in pacemakers and defibrillators-the 
      value of atrial electrograms.
PG  - 2048-2051
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.03.38 [doi]
AB  - Today's pacemakers and defibrillators include diagnostic tools for detecting and 
      treating cardiac arrhythmias like silent atrial fibrillation as atrial high rate 
      episodes (AHREs). This diagnostic capability is crucial to prevent the potential 
      embolic complications this AHREs are related to. However, sometimes data 
      retrieved from diagnostic counters may be misleading reflecting limitations of 
      detection algorithms, which must follow mathematical rules to classify events on 
      a beat-to-beat basis. The incorporation of stored electrograms has been an 
      important milestone in improving the diagnostic capabilities of these devices 
      confirming the arrhythmia diagnosis.
