TI  - Transvenous phrenic nerve stimulation, a novel therapeutic approach for central 
      sleep apnea.
PG  - 2005-2010
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2018.03.59 [doi]
AB  - Central sleep apnea (CSA) is common in heart failure (HF) patients. Traditional 
      treatment of CSA, including continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP), adaptive 
      servo ventilation (ASV), oxygen therapy, and CO(2) inhalation, has respective 
      limitations. Transvenous phrenic nerve stimulation (PNS), a novel therapeutic 
      approach for CSA, was proved to be effective and safe. The remedē(®) system and 
      related transvenous PNS methods was approved by FDA in 2017, for treating 
      moderate to severe CSA.
