TI  - Enhanced recovery pathways in thoracic surgery from Italian VATS group: nursing 
      care program.
PG  - S529-S534
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.12.85 [doi]
AB  - Enhanced recovery after surgery (ERAS) is an interprofessional program that can 
      lead to hastened patient recovery and reduced time in hospital. Nursing staff 
      play a key role in the implementation of enhanced recovery protocols. This issue 
      focalizes the role of nurses in ERAS program for patients submitted to Thoracic 
      Surgery, in particular for cases of major lung resection performed by a minimally 
      invasive surgical approach (VATS, video assisted thoracic surgery).
