TI  - Approach to resection of sternoclavicular tumor abutting the common carotid 
      artery in irradiated field.
PG  - E38-E41
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.12.60 [doi]
AB  - Head and neck cancer recurrence at the sternoclavicular junction (SCJ) in 
      irradiated field poses a special challenge in terms of surgical planning. We 
      herein present a case of tonsillar squamous cell cancer recurrence at the SCJ in 
      a patient with history of tracheostomy and head and neck radiation. We describe 
      our preoperative planning for vascular control and possible reconstruction as 
      well as our approach for safe resection.
