TI  - Different QRS morphologies in a dual-chamber pacemaker: what is the mechanism?
PG  - 4674-4675
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.10.90 [doi]
AB  - A 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG) of a dual-chamber pacemaker with different 
      paced QRS morphologies is presented. Such an observation is usually made when 
      there are different degrees of fusion, in association with the intrinsic rhythm 
      in the presence of spontaneous changes of the stimulation mode of the pacemaker.
