TI  - Prevention of cardiac herniation and left artery descending obstruction in cases 
      of extensive surgical pericardial window procedure.
PG  - 4597-4598
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.10.37 [doi]
AB  - The thoracotomy approach for pericardial window surgery was shown to be more 
      effective at preventing effusion recurrence and the need for repeat surgery. 
      However, cardiac herniation remains a common complication after extensive 
      pericardial excision. This technical note describes a simple and effective 
      technique to prevent potential heart herniation through the pericardial window 
      and at the same time to avoid potential obstruction of the left artery 
      descending.
