TI  - Chondroblastoma of the rib in a 47-year-old man: a case report with a systematic 
      review of literature.
PG  - E907-E911
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.137 [doi]
AB  - Chondroblastoma is an uncommon benign bone tumour arising typically in the 
      epiphysis. Few cases of chondroblastoma of the rib have been reported in the 
      literature. We describe a case of chondroblastoma of a 47-year-old man located in 
      the body of the IX right rib. The patient presented a moderate right thoracic 
      pain with an apparently palpable mass. Computed tomography (CT) scan showed a 
      well-defined oval 49 mm × 43 mm lesion with the lytic bone destruction of the 
      rib. A surgical resection was performed with an excellent outcome and no 
      recurrence after 4-year follow-up. We also conducted a systematic review of 
      literature where we evidenced that chondroblastoma could affect people of all 
      age, but it's most common in children and young adult. Surgical resection 
      constitutes the treatment of choice.
