DP  - 2017 Sep
TI  - Adult-onset Langerhans cell histiocytosis of the sternum.
PG  - E783-E786
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.51 [doi]
AB  - Langerhans cell histiocytosis (LCH) is a rare disease with uncertain etiology 
      that is more prevalent in children. LCH typically invades skeletal systems, but 
      in rare cases, it has been reported in the ribs or sternum. Optimal treatment 
      choices for single-site, skeletal LCH are still undefined. We report a case of 
      adult-onset LCH of the sternum. The range of surrounding soft tissue invasion was 
      confirmed by three-dimensional fusion and reconstruction of chest computed 
      tomography and magnetic resonance images. Our patient was successfully treated by 
      local surgical curettage and adjuvant radiation therapy. We concluded that 
      postoperative adjuvant radiation therapy may be advantageous for single-site LCH 
      of bones with soft tissue invasion.
