TI  - The role of sympathectomy in long QT syndrome.
PG  - 3394-3397
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.45 [doi]
AB  - Long QT syndrome (LQTS) is an uncommon and potentially fatal cardiac 
      channelopathy. Treatment options can be medical with β-blockers or surgical with 
      implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD) implantations and left cardiac 
      sympathetic denervation (LCSD). Purpose of this paper is through a literature 
      review to identify the management algorithm and the role of sympathectomy in 
      LQTS.
