DP  - 2017 Sep
TI  - Recipient selection process and listing for lung transplantation.
PG  - 3372-3384
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.90 [doi]
AB  - Lung transplantation remains the ultimate treatment option for selected patients 
      with end-stage (cardio) pulmonary disease. Given the current organ shortage, it 
      is without any doubt that careful selection of potential transplant candidates is 
      essential as this may greatly influence survival after the procedure. In this 
      paper, we will review the current guidelines for referral and listing of lung 
      transplant candidates in general, and in more depth for the specific underlying 
      diseases. Needless to state that these are not absolute guidelines, and that 
      decisions depend upon center's activity, waiting list, etc. Therefore, every 
      patient should be discussed with the transplant center before any definite 
      decision is made to accept or decline a patient for lung transplantation.
