DP  - 2017 Sep
TI  - Cystic tumor of the atrioventricular node: a review of the literature.
PG  - 3313-3318
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.08.101 [doi]
AB  - Primary cardiac tumors are uncommon clinical entities with an incidence of 
      0.0017% to 0.03% of all autopsies. Cystic tumor of the atrioventricular (AV) 
      node, also known as mesothelioma of the AV node, is a benign congenital tumor 
      that is located in the triangle of Koch in the AV nodal region of the atrial 
      septum of the heart. It comprises of 2.7% of cardiac tumors and is the most 
      common primary cardiac tumor causing sudden death. We herein review the etiology, 
      presentation, differential diagnosis, diagnosis, management, surgical approaches 
      and outcomes of this rare tumor.
