VI  - 9
IP  - Suppl 8
DP  - 2017 Jul
TI  - Enhanced recovery protocols after oesophagectomy.
PG  - S781-S784
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.07.16 [doi]
AB  - The feasibility and safety of enhanced recovery protocols (ERP) have been 
      demonstrated in a large number of surgical specialties. Several studies have 
      shown improved post-operative outcomes and economic benefit from the use of ERPs 
      in oesophageal cancer surgery. However, these improvements are not always 
      translated more widely into clinical practice due to variation in protocols, poor 
      compliance and failure to implement a robust implementation strategy. ERP 
      implementation strategies should reflect the fact that these are complex 
      interventions that are influenced by a wide range of social, organizational and 
      cultural factors.
