TI  - Double pseudoaneurysm, recurrent subvalvular aortic membrane and small left 
      ventricular outflow tract in the same patient: who dares?
PG  - S547-S550
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.05.03 [doi]
AB  - Patients with pseudoaneurysm in the left ventricular outflow tract (LVOT) 
      commonly present vague and nonspecific symptoms making the diagnosis difficult. 
      We present the case of a 37-year-old patient with two subvalvular pseudoaneurysms 
      in whom a combined resection surgery, enlargement of the LVOT, aortic valve 
      replacement (AVR) and aortic root replacement were performed using the technique 
      of Cabrol.
