TI  - Imaging for surveillance and operative management for endovascular aortic 
      aneurysm repairs.
PG  - S309-S316
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.03.89 [doi]
AB  - Endovascular aortic aneurysm repairs rely heavily on radiologic imaging 
      modalities for preoperative surveillance, intraoperative management, and 
      postoperative follow-up. Ultrasonography, computed tomography (CT), magnetic 
      resonance imaging (MRI) and angiography all have utility at different stages of 
      management. Often one imaging modality compliments another by providing 
      supplementary information. Data from the imaging exams must be synthesized into 
      one coherent plan for managing patients with aortic aneurysms.
