TI  - Use of CO(2) in video assisted thoracic surgery and single-lumen endotracheal 
      tube-a new less invasive approach.
PG  - 903-906
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2017.01.53 [doi]
AB  - Carbon dioxide (CO(2)) has been extensively used to allow laparoscopic 
      procedures, due to its extensive advantages in obtaining a fairly innocuous 
      pneumoperitoneum to allow visceral dissection. Its use in video assisted thoracic 
      surgery (VATS) has seldom been described. We present our experience in more than 
      100 patients, operated for various thoracic pathologies, in whom we created a 
      surgical pneumothorax to allow different surgeries to be undertaken.
