TI  - Study designs in thoracic surgery research.
PG  - E932-E934
AB  - In this short review, we'll try to specify the differences between evaluation 
      procedures of groups of data, as they present to researchers. The way and time 
      data are gathered defines the type of study is going to shape. When we observe a 
      cluster of data without deliberately interfering with the process we mean to 
      evaluate, we perform an observational study. Observational studies are the main 
      topic of this issue. Upon the contrary, experimental studies imply the direct 
      action of the observer on the study population in order to define the role of a 
      given exposure. The topic of experimental study design will be covered in another 
      issue of this series.
