DP  - 2016 Sep
TI  - Developing miRNA therapeutics for cardiac repair in ischemic heart disease.
PG  - E918-E927
AB  - MicroRNAs (miRNAs) families have been found to be powerful regulators in a wide 
      variety of diseases, which enables the possible use of miRNAs in therapeutic 
      strategies for cardiac repair after ischemic heart disease. This review provides 
      some general insights into miRNAs modulation for development of current molecular 
      and cellular therapeutics in cardiac repair, including endogenous regeneration, 
      endogenous repair, stem cells transplantation, and reprogramming. We also review 
      the delivery strategies for miRNAs modulation, and briefly summarize the current 
      bench and clinical efforts that are being made to explore miRNAs as the future 
      therapeutic target.
