TI  - Bioresorbable vascular scaffolds in patients with acute myocardial infarction: a 
      new step forward to optimized reperfusion?
PG  - E417-23
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.03.75 [doi]
AB  - Bioresorbable vascular scaffolds (BVS) represent a disruptive technology that has 
      caused a new revolution in interventional cardiology. BVS appear to be 
      particularly appealing in patients presenting with an acute myocardial infarction 
      (MI). The available evidence on the value of BVS implantation in this challenging 
      scenario is very promising but still limited. Results come from preliminary small 
      observational studies, prospective registries that include a control group, and 
      from scarce randomized clinical trials with surrogate mechanistic or angiographic 
      primary end-points. Further studies, powered for clinical endpoints, are required 
      to establish the relative safety and efficacy of BVS vs. new-generation metallic 
      drug-eluting stents (DES) in patients with ST-segment elevation acute MI.
