TI  - Dimethylacetamide-induced occupational toxic hepatitis with a short term 
      recurrence: a rare case report.
PG  - E408-11
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.04.44 [doi]
AB  - In recent years, N,N-dimethylacetamide (DMAc) is widely used in the textile and 
      plastics industry as a solvent alternative to more toxic N,N-dimethylformamide 
      (DMF). At home and abroad, sporadic group case reports have revealed that DMAc 
      could cause toxic hepatitis and symptoms or signs indicative of liver involvement 
      among workers exposed to DMAc, with severe cases leading to death. This paper 
      reports a rare case of severe acute toxic hepatitis with a short term recurrence 
      induced by occupational contact with DMAc in a polyimide film factory, as well as 
      in-depth analysis via relevant information and literature.
