DP  - 2016 Jun
TI  - Tumor-to-tumor metastasis: an unusual case of breast cancer metastatic to a 
      solitary fibrous tumor.
PG  - E374-8
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.03.79 [doi]
AB  - Solitary fibrous tumor (SFT) is a rare mesenchymal neoplasm that most commonly 
      involves the visceral or parietal pleura, but that has also been described 
      arising from virtually all organs. This neoplasm exhibits rich vascularity, a 
      characteristic it shares with renal cell carcinoma, making these tumors 
      especially suitable for harboring metastases. We present a case of a 64-year-old 
      woman with history of right breast cancer treated six years previously and who 
      presents with a left pulmonary SFT containing metastatic invasive ductal breast 
      carcinoma as well as a synchronous contralateral primary adenocarcinoma of the 
      lung. The literature on tumor-to-tumor metastasis is then reviewed.
