DP  - 2016 May
TI  - Acute respiratory distress syndrome caused by Mycoplasma pneumoniae without 
      elevated pulmonary vascular permeability: a case report.
PG  - E319-24
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.03.08 [doi]
AB  - Sporadic patients with acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) caused by 
      Mycoplasma pneumoniae have been reported. However, knowledge about the 
      pathophysiology and pharmacological treatment of this condition is insufficient. 
      Moreover, the pulmonary vascular permeability in ARDS related to M. pneumoniae 
      infection has not been reported. We report a case of ARDS caused by Mycoplasma 
      pneumoniae without elevated pulmonary vascular permeability, which was 
      successfully treated using low-dose short-term hydrocortisone, suggesting that 
      pulmonary infiltration in ARDS caused by Mycoplasma pneumoniae does not match the 
      criteria of permeability edema observed in typical ARDS.
