TI  - Strategy analysis of cardiopulmonary resuscitation training in the community.
PG  - E160-5
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.06.09 [doi]
AB  - Bystander cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) is a crucial therapy for sudden 
      cardiac arrest. This appreciation produced immense efforts by professional 
      organizations to train laypeople for CPR skills. However, the rate of CPR 
      training is low and varies widely across communities. Several strategies are used 
      in order to improve the rate of CPR training and are performed in some advanced 
      countries. The Chinese CPR training in communities could gain enlightenment from 
      them.
