VI  - 7
IP  - 3
DP  - 2015 Mar
TI  - Aberrant aneurysm of adult-type pulmonary sequestration: report of a case.
PG  - E33-6
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.02.15 [doi]
AB  - Aberrant pulmonary artery exposed by high-blood pressure over a long period in 
      adult-type pulmonary sequestration can be susceptible to arteriosclerotic change 
      and aneurysmal formation. Dividing this aneurysmal artery has a risk of stump 
      leakage and aneurysm. We herein report a 64-year-old man with an aberrant 
      aneurysm of intralobar pulmonary sequestration. Thoracoscopic resection of the 
      sequestrated lung was performed uneventfully by prior endovascular occlusion of 
      the aberrant aneurysm.
