VI  - 7
IP  - 2
DP  - 2015 Feb
TI  - Are the novel anticoagulants better than warfarin for patients with atrial 
      fibrillation?
PG  - 165-71
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2015.01.23 [doi]
AB  - Atrial fibrillation (AF) is associated with significant morbidity and mortality 
      related to stroke due to thromboembolism. Several novel oral anticoagulants 
      (NOACs) have been developed that dose-dependently inhibit thrombin or activated 
      factor X (factor Xa). These new agents offer potential advantages over vitamin K 
      antagonists, however, several limitations exist. We will review the four large 
      randomized trials comparing the efficacy and safety of new oral anticoagulants 
      with warfarin for stroke prevention in patients with AF as well as assess "real 
      world" data and discuss the limitations of the new agents.
